[[{"str":"Matching Sentences Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.67506332,"width":360.680512359636,"height":18.015113279999998},{"str":"","x":190.65994887999997,"y":708.63728012,"width":0,"height":14.0067505752},{"str":"Guitar storage and maintenance","x":190.65994887999997,"y":708.63728012,"width":214.0060688586218,"height":14.0067505752},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":674.85894272,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Properly maintaining a valuable guitar keeps it valuable. Guitars can take a lot of","x":72.06045311999999,"y":674.85894272,"width":451.2105655387233,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"abuse, especially if you play live shows and tour, and even if it pretty much \"sounds","x":72.06045311999999,"y":658.34508888,"width":451.79113060769754,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the same”, lack of maintenance may suddenly render the instrument unplayable. You","x":72.06045311999999,"y":641.83123504,"width":451.23402271747347,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"don't need to carefully examine a guitar every day, but occasional check-ups keep it","x":72.06045311999999,"y":625.3173812,"width":451.59760529500005,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"sounding good and ready to play.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":608.80352736,"width":177.61775653419394,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The easiest way to take care of your guitar is to store it properly. The more","x":72.06045311999999,"y":586.28463576,"width":451.29852799238614,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"expensive the guitar, the better your storage should be. It is generally accepted that","x":72.06045311999999,"y":569.77078192,"width":451.492051623673,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the air humidity should be neither too high nor too low, thus somewhere in the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":553.2569280800001,"width":451.53896411961114,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"45-55% range, and the temperature of the area should be about 65-75 °F (18-24 °C).","x":72.06045311999999,"y":536.7430742399999,"width":451.5096407996247,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"These two factors are the biggest threat to an instrument, because changes in","x":72.06045311999999,"y":520.2292204,"width":451.29852811248685,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"moisture and temperature can cause permanent warping of the neck and other","x":72.06045311999999,"y":503.71536656,"width":451.6445194723488,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"critical parts. For guitars made out of solid wood, it is advisable to use a humidifier to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":487.20151272000004,"width":451.4920516837231,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"prevent cracks and damage from weather change. On the other hand, guitars made","x":72.06045311999999,"y":470.68765888,"width":451.3982209870608,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"out","x":72.06045311999999,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":16.69564687022434,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":88.75609999022433,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":10.437500640000007,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"of","x":96.59079817312735,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":106.60701343932699,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":10.43750007999998,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"multi-layered","x":114.44171120187735,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":68.7471263363232,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":183.18883753820057,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":10.43750487999997,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"(plywood)","x":191.02353890377358,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":52.06320802544868,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":243.08674692922233,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":10.437495279999915,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"wood, typically in budget guitars, can withstand","x":250.92144108875,"y":454.17380504000005,"width":272.83630827921223,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"relatively more humidity and temperature changes. Keeping the guitar in a case","x":72.06045311999999,"y":437.6599512,"width":451.1343278011865,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"away from direct sunlight can help with increasing the life of the guitar.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":421.14609736000006,"width":373.1743908327151,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The surest way to keep your guitar in good shape is to remember this simple rule:","x":72.06045311999999,"y":398.62720576000004,"width":451.16365112117296,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Do not expose the guitar to any climate condition that you would not want to be","x":72.06045311999999,"y":382.11335192,"width":451.4685907217995,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"exposed to. If you keep this in mind, your instrument will likely last years and years.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":365.59949808000005,"width":441.90392445011395,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Avoid large or rapid changes in humidity. Like your body, the guitar gets used to the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":343.08060648000003,"width":451.3864887045878,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"climate it is in, and suddenly changing it causes stress. Humidity is the most","x":72.06045311999999,"y":326.56675264,"width":451.1460526374126,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"dangerous thing that attacks an instrument, because when wood gets wet, the cell","x":72.06045311999999,"y":310.0528988000001,"width":451.6562463502882,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"walls become softer and it is more easily bent. Often, the strings themselves are","x":72.06045311999999,"y":293.53904496000007,"width":451.4099477448993,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"enough to bend the neck. Also, if the humidity stays very low, then the wood will","x":72.06045311999999,"y":277.02519112000004,"width":451.6093376975742,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"crack and the structure will weaken.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":260.51133728,"width":190.24358322157033,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Temperature on its own is less damaging to the guitar. Wood is generally tolerant to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":237.99244568000006,"width":451.2750671505628,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"changes in temperature, and for the most part it expands and contracts together.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":221.47859184000004,"width":451.14019376227185,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Extreme temperatures or rapid temperature changes, however, can cause serious","x":72.06045311999999,"y":204.964738,"width":451.70902486736213,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"damage, especially when combined with extreme humidity. Changes in temperature","x":72.06045311999999,"y":188.4508841600001,"width":451.22229379782107,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"also affect strings, especially nylon strings. A significant change in temperature","x":72.06045311999999,"y":171.93703032000008,"width":451.5330995396843,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"typically detunes the strings. Other areas to watch for temperature-related damage","x":72.06045311999999,"y":155.42317648000005,"width":451.29266359261044,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"are any glued joins, like where the neck meets the body, or the fretboard attaches to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":138.90932264000003,"width":451.0522277055868,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the neck.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":122.3954688,"width":48.73815292262357,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Never expose your instrument to extreme temperatures for a long time. For instance,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":99.87657720000004,"width":451.33957801016066,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"leaving your guitar in a car in the summer all day, or leaving it outside overnight are","x":72.06045311999999,"y":83.36272336000002,"width":451.5976051748994,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32997792000003,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Note: This is not a real IELTS test. This practice test is to give you an opportunity to practise","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32997792000003,"width":444.120631174785,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"implementing the strategies from the course. It does not reflect the scores, time needed or","x":72.06045311999999,"y":30.068013240000028,"width":444.4724880753799,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"level of difficulty of a real IELTS test.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":15.806048560000022,"width":176.13409149452846,"height":12.01007552}],[{"str":"Matching Sentences Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.67503776,"width":360.680512359636,"height":18.015113279999998},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88914372,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"sure ways to completely destroy your instrument. Also keep the guitar out of direct","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88914372,"width":451.5917427567863,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"sunlight as much as possible, because it makes the wood more brittle and can","x":72.06045311999999,"y":694.3752898800001,"width":451.19296699491275,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"change the color of the instrument.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":677.8614360400001,"width":184.93053202451915,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Keeping your instrument strung and in tune is another good way to make sure that","x":72.06045311999999,"y":655.34254444,"width":451.5565532355125,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"you don't harm your instrument. Strings put tension on the neck. Excessive tension","x":72.06045311999999,"y":638.8286906000001,"width":451.4979139817357,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"may make the neck bow if the guitar isn't kept in tune.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":622.3148367599999,"width":285.3448496733423,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"In terms of maintenance, it is important to consider that the body often takes the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":599.79594516,"width":451.6093356558614,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"most abuse, simply because it is the biggest target. To help keep a fine instrument in","x":72.06045311999999,"y":583.2820913200001,"width":451.36303723062343,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"good condition, wipe it down with a soft cloth after playing. Don't use water-based","x":72.06045311999999,"y":566.7682374799999,"width":451.6738426722346,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"furniture sprays. You can buy specially treated cloths and sprays for guitars at","x":72.06045311999999,"y":550.25438364,"width":451.4334049836997,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"almost any music store. Dirt, sweat, and often small nicks and scrapes can just be","x":72.06045311999999,"y":533.7405298000001,"width":451.6503857336866,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"cleaned up with a cloth and a little bit of warm water. Murphy's Oil Soap can be used","x":72.06045311999999,"y":517.22667596,"width":451.1401882976872,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"to clean the whole guitar. Wipe the strings with a clean cloth. Some guitarists","x":72.06045311999999,"y":500.71282212000006,"width":451.33957428703707,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"advocate wiping the strings with warm water, but be sure to protect the fingerboard","x":72.06045311999999,"y":484.19896828000014,"width":451.1988347575093,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"from moisture. Consider wiping your guitar strings off every time you play because","x":72.06045311999999,"y":467.68511444,"width":451.49791206012355,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"oils and dirt left on your strings make them asymmetrical—as opposed to evenly","x":72.06045311999999,"y":451.1712606000001,"width":451.41581016301245,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"cylindrical vibrating bodies. They may even wear out a bit faster. A soft, natural fiber","x":72.06045311999999,"y":434.65740675999996,"width":451.1753759573992,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"or microfiber cloth works the best and is safest for the finish. Clean the frets as you","x":72.06045311999999,"y":418.14355292000005,"width":451.1519225618232,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"do the rest of the guitar. If necessary, carefully use 0.001 steel wool to get grime off","x":72.06045311999999,"y":401.62969908000014,"width":451.5213731421481,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the fingerboard next to the frets. You can also gently go over the frets to take off any","x":72.06045311999999,"y":385.11584524,"width":451.7148948518232,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"minor nicks.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":368.6019914000001,"width":64.06741926577378,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"If you have a stained or lacquered body, you can treat it with a little bit of furniture","x":72.06045311999999,"y":346.0830998000001,"width":451.35717271074674,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"polish. However, if you have a guitar with an untreated body, be extremely careful","x":72.06045311999999,"y":329.56924596,"width":451.20470113894766,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"with polish. For these types, it is better to find some sort of cleaning oil or wax, since","x":72.06045311999999,"y":313.0553921200001,"width":451.7324877508984,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"they help prevent hair-line cracks from developing. After cleaning, the body must be","x":72.06045311999999,"y":296.54153828000017,"width":451.3806244249126,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"absolutely dry, because if the wood gets over-moistened, the tone of the guitar will","x":72.06045311999999,"y":280.02768444000003,"width":451.55069099755065,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"begin to degrade.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":263.5138306000001,"width":93.48858533764641,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":240.99493900000016,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Source:","x":72.06045311999999,"y":240.99493900000016,"width":41.39019175424906,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":113.45064487424905,"y":240.99493900000016,"width":4.445313199999988,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Guitar/Guitar_Maintenance_and_Storage","x":116.78742907687734,"y":240.99493900000016,"width":371.8490602633653,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":191.45337747999997,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Questions 1-10","x":72.06045311999999,"y":191.45337747999997,"width":86.0995740914468,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":174.93952364000006,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Complete each sentence with the correct ending","x":72.06045311999999,"y":174.93952364000006,"width":257.03203498214265,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":329.09248810214274,"y":174.93952364000006,"width":4.445316559999861,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"A-O","x":332.4292748268868,"y":174.93952364000006,"width":22.014562226849808,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":354.4438370537366,"y":174.93952364000006,"width":4.445307519999927,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"from the box below.","x":357.78061699278805,"y":174.93952364000006,"width":104.8066741745969,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":158.42566980000015,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"NB","x":72.06045311999999,"y":158.42566980000015,"width":17.346583715650187,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":89.40703683565019,"y":158.42566980000015,"width":4.445312439999983,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"not all letters will be used.","x":92.74382046779989,"y":158.42566980000015,"width":137.51770991144681,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":125.3979621200001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"1.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":125.3979621200001,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":125.3979621200001,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"One advantage of the correct maintenance of a guitar is that","x":85.41345210842489,"y":125.3979621200001,"width":319.79758055706475,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":108.88410827999996,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"2.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":108.88410827999996,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":108.88410827999996,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Even though the sound a guitar makes may not deteriorate,","x":85.41345210842489,"y":108.88410827999996,"width":315.79226733053997,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":92.37025444000005,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"3.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":92.37025444000005,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":92.37025444000005,"width":4.4453130799999965,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The most serious dangers to a guitar are","x":85.41345249875235,"y":92.37025444000005,"width":216.2927798331181,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":75.85640060000014,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"4.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":75.85640060000014,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":75.85640060000014,"width":4.4453130799999965,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"If the material the guitar is made out of is a multi-layered wood,","x":85.41345249875235,"y":75.85640060000014,"width":334.4407244968406,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32995236000011,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Note: This is not a real IELTS test. This practice test is to give you an opportunity to practise","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32995236000011,"width":444.120631174785,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"implementing the strategies from the course. It does not reflect the scores, time needed or","x":72.06045311999999,"y":30.067987679999987,"width":444.4724880753799,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"level of difficulty of a real IELTS test.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":15.806023000000096,"width":176.13409149452846,"height":12.01007552}],[{"str":"Matching Sentences Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.6750122000001,"width":360.680512359636,"height":18.015113279999998},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88911816,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"5.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88911816,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":710.88911816,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The reason that humidity poses such a risk to guitars is that","x":85.41345210842489,"y":710.88911816,"width":316.41974705726625,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":694.37526432,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"6.","x